1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,080
I sell business training to business clients.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:06,320
So last year we did 14.8 million.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:08,600
Bad ass, what do you teach them how to do?

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:09,840
Teach them how to grow their business.

5
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:12,280
Is it courses that are done in person or is it digital?

6
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,840
We have the in-person model

7
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:15,920
and we want to scale to 25 million,

8
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:20,320
run 12 to 15 live in-person events on a monthly basis,

9
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,160
which are three events.

10
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,800
Right now who's doing the pitching at the events?

11
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,200
So I've got about six to eight people that I've trained

12
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,380
and we've got some really good ones,

13
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:29,680
but it does take a long time to get those people

14
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,840
up to speed to be able to do a really good job.

15
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:33,640
Well, let me ask you a question about the pitching.

16
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:36,320
So when you have the pitch, is there a slide deck?

17
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,280
Yeah, yeah.

18
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:38,440
How many slides is it?

19
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,840
268 for the day.

20
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:42,640
Yeah, yeah, for the whole day?

21
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,480
Yeah, for the day.

22
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,400
Ah, all right.

23
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:46,720
So let me just make your life a hundred times easier

24
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,840
for six days of work.

25
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:52,840
So the pitch should be word for word scripted on the slides.

26
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,960
So my pitch at Money Models, the book launch,

27
00:00:55,960 --> 00:01:00,320
was 1,700 slides just for the 90 minute presentation

28
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,160
that I gave, which means every word I said

29
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:04,000
was on the screen paired with a visual

30
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,520
for people who don't speak English that good.

31
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:07,880
The only thing that you need to train them on

32
00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:10,920
is how fast to say the words, how loudly to say it,

33
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:12,940
when to raise their voice and when to lower it

34
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:14,440
and what to do with their hands.

